# Secrets — never commit
#
# Unanchored on purpose: these match at ANY depth, not just infra/. A stray copy
# of .env landing at the repo root — a mistyped cp, a script whose relative path
# resolved against the wrong working directory — is otherwise untracked,
# unignored, and one `git add -A` away from being published. That has already
# happened once here.
#
# .env.example is a distinct filename and stays tracked.
.env
# Timestamped .env backups taken before config changes hold the same real
# secrets as .env itself.
.env.bak-*
*.env.local
.claude/settings.local.json
*.pem
*.key

# Runtime
node_modules/
.DS_Store
backups/
